{"title":"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallelogram\" title=\"Parallelogram\">parallelogram</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diagonal\" title=\"Diagonal\">diagonals</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />. Angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/9/459b39e026037707282c95dfdbfd6dc64c855a16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00cb04571fd7efc09d2de1b2da589ee6a5b7756d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBC$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> are each twice as large as angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/600c2c8bf2070476b38b1f452ef77d07759219f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBA$\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />, and angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/21361fc8f29984fa3e95bfc0e578efdbce08c736.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> times as large as angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd97737c9a1eb5146725902d4e4c4bda1388129b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca04a9e4a27988d65b60bf8e295958a90b3dc74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor 1000r \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(trigonometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (trigonometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(trigonometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (trigonometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_1_.28trigonometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(trigonometry)\">Solution 1 (trigonometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (trigonometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/9/d09e1f91df6f1a2f004955349478e82b4cf67dad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(180); pathpen = black+linewidth(0.7); pair B=(0,0), A=expi(pi/4), C=IP(A--A + 2*expi(17*pi/12), B--(3,0)), D=A+C, O=IP(A--C,B--D);  D(MP(&quot;A&quot;,A,N)--MP(&quot;B&quot;,B)--MP(&quot;C&quot;,C)--MP(&quot;D&quot;,D,N)--cycle); D(B--D); D(A--C); D(MP(&quot;O&quot;,O,SE)); D(anglemark(D,B,A,4));D(anglemark(B,A,C,3.5));D(anglemark(B,A,C,4.5));D(anglemark(C,B,D,3.5));D(anglemark(C,B,D,4.5));  [/asy]\" width=\"302\" height=\"205\" /></center>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/b/dcbcbf54cf3a55ebab993bdcfa61764d0861e098.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\angle DBA$\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/760f5c3e3493a49d23fa6463f62c2d3028d34845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAB = \\angle DBC = 2\\theta$\" width=\"179\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e335d87f31a6a5a5246a79e4658c1b6510afc291.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOB = 180 - 3\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"147\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/f/73f7bb470d30590bbedb92233f80485789e84d68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB = 180 - 5\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"146\" height=\"13\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a parallelogram, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbbdc4b83b4c947098e1137d39af9df0aa53fbaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA = OC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Sines\" title=\"Law of Sines\">Law of Sines</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/4/424f1a279c4d095032f323c257354f7307ae51b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABO,\\, \\triangle BCO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"128\" height=\"17\" />,\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/5/c45cc618c84f220b8d2b555f9a4961f1716b91e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sin \\angle CBO}{OC} = \\frac{\\sin \\angle ACB}{OB} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\frac{\\sin \\angle DBA}{OC} = \\frac{\\sin \\angle BAC}{OB}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"453\" height=\"38\" /></center>\n<p>Dividing the two equalities yields \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a1749253b72959969f81abbf6f1d255bf750f7a1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sin 2\\theta}{\\sin \\theta} = \\frac{\\sin (180 - 5\\theta)}{\\sin 2\\theta} \\Longrightarrow \\sin^2 2\\theta = \\sin 5\\theta \\sin \\theta.\\]\" width=\"376\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Pythagorean and product-to-sum identities yield\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/3/5331157cc39adc248998d798812f41eb212a2bdb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 - \\cos^2 2 \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 4\\theta - \\cos 6 \\theta}{2},\\]\" width=\"228\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>and the double and triple angle (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c01905f82fbeab8f1b87e41ec88096d6937d729e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 3x = 4\\cos^3 x - 3\\cos x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"200\" height=\"15\" />) formulas further simplify this to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/7/367929cc5ab370f997c8cfd544a4af84c2c9fab8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4\\cos^3 2\\theta - 4\\cos^2 2\\theta - 3\\cos 2\\theta + 3 = (4\\cos^2 2\\theta - 3)(\\cos 2\\theta - 1) = 0\\]\" width=\"481\" height=\"19\" /> \n</p><p>The only value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that fits in this context comes from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/e/8ee66018b550830249a8e456a25d26aace8b96c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\cos^2 2\\theta - 3 = 0 \\Longrightarrow \\cos 2\\theta = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\Longrightarrow \\theta = 15^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"364\" height=\"41\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/2391dfcc72cc81b175f8823fe1e60132a5a98617.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor 1000r \\rfloor = \\left\\lfloor 1000 \\cdot \\frac{180 - 5\\theta}{180 - 3\\theta} \\right\\rfloor = \\left \\lfloor \\frac{7000}{9} \\right \\rfloor = \\boxed{777}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"376\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_2_.28trigonometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(trigonometry)\">Solution 2 (trigonometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (trigonometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as above. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/a/05a108c0cb5d5b2d0cbe9b7d0662a5ddcdf7c8c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAB = \\angle CBO$\" width=\"135\" height=\"13\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/6/746668cb64573fb77a677cecafe0616a49b8b5a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle COB \\sim \\triangle CBA$\" width=\"142\" height=\"13\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/5/595db6e072db7c130eb248845e4295e74f68d042.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CO}{BC} = \\frac{BC}{AC} \\Longrightarrow BC^2 = AC \\cdot CO = 2CO^2 \\Longrightarrow BC = CO\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"475\" height=\"37\" />. The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Sines\" title=\"Law of Sines\">Law of Sines</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/41752e67cd033c961edd7532c9376bc82296d255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BOC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> yields that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/0/7c05021ce15cb9b41fee79aa271c32959a5bff0d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{BC}{CO} = \\frac{\\sin (180-3\\theta)}{\\sin 2\\theta} = \\frac{\\sin 3\\theta}{\\sin 2\\theta} = \\sqrt{2}\\]\" width=\"284\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Expanding using the sine double and triple angle formulas, we have \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/9/f9958dbd23dbddd1e099e28698bf5d3bc05f422e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\sqrt {2} \\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta = \\sin\\theta( - 4\\sin ^2 \\theta + 3) \\Longrightarrow \\sin \\theta\\left(4\\cos^2\\theta - 2\\sqrt {2} \\cos \\theta - 1\\right) = 0.\\]\" width=\"591\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_formula\" title=\"Quadratic formula\">quadratic formula</a>, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/e/a9e2e0341476f8a38dc60537997adc2bcb088584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta = \\frac {2\\sqrt {2} \\pm \\sqrt {8 + 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 4}}{8} = \\frac {\\sqrt {6} \\pm \\sqrt {2}}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"321\" height=\"43\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/5/4d5731cfcea82aabdc7bd9a7b97420bc6e233acc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = 15^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> (as the other roots are too large to make sense in context). The answer follows as above.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We will focus on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/8/ea8548c45e5466feeaa293de8f1e94a9d3a8adf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABO = x$\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/d/fedbf3bf070cdc9ac9f4dbcf2c8be34019976152.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAO = \\angle OBC = 2x$\" width=\"179\" height=\"13\" />. Draw the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular\" title=\"Perpendicular\">perpendicular</a> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> intersecting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Without_loss_of_generality\" title=\"Without loss of generality\">Without loss of generality</a>, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/6/ea6cad1d9821c71bbe259f7e6858b3952e8dfe14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO = CO = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"113\" height=\"13\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0acc61d1be5fd33e0277ec7ae18a20277e1f5fd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HO = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumcenter\" title=\"Circumcenter\">circumcenter</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/4/64417acfe8647838193695cb07a948da232b5572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AHC$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/7/697aec2b715044cbedca790011912ce22a03226c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OHA = 2x$\" width=\"100\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>By the Exterior Angle Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11c039b8316d0d4678898a32db15618f459d59f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle COB = 3x$\" width=\"99\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/105bf055e8dbaa56f2aa39a7d1a38bb8f4698766.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle COH = 4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"104\" height=\"14\" />. That implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edfabd9c36f9fb9e9d7b2b5933f41e9a5a2e4e89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle HOB = x$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" />. That makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/a/16a9bfbecfef5fd7fe63383eba62ffb7bcdaee83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HO = HB = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" />. Then since by AA (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef1b9896d347c9b3b0df611421a895ff88ef44fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle HBC = \\angle HOC = 3x$\" width=\"184\" height=\"12\" /> and reflexive on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30eda2a3ddcee9f2f9faaa7cc3629e003c2e3cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OCB$\" width=\"55\" height=\"12\" />), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/1/091bf9b1e011632c70c738fd326b6c5604c8a613.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OCB \\sim \\triangle BCA$\" width=\"142\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/6/8b64d0330d044a95b98d2f79590db3e51384ef77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {CO}{BC} = \\frac {BC}{AC} \\implies 2 = BC^2 = \\implies BC = \\sqrt {2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"354\" height=\"37\" /></center>\n<p>Then by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ffd09708acae6437fe0241503b1583a57a6f1c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2 + HC^2 = \\left(\\sqrt {2}\\right)^2\\implies HC = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"267\" height=\"35\" />. That makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/b/17b31bb2aa333e75611b85739a3d205ceb996e10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle HOC$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> equilateral. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/9/389e7a94e3e3b0912bf219ce0708b0963bbe0304.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle HOC = 4x = 60 \\implies x = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"246\" height=\"13\" />. The answer follows as above. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME\" title=\"1996 AIME\">1996 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1996 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1996\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Final Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a h